1
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:10,880
YUM! YUM!

2
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,437
YUM! YUM! YUM !YUM! YUM!

3
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:15,350
YUM!

4
00:00:15,433 --> 00:00:16,263
YUM!!

5
00:00:16,346 --> 00:00:17,574
Are you King of Kings?

6
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:08,277
I can read your mind, and I see
you're losing hope, Wheeler.

7
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:12,317
As long as Esperoba has Ginzo on the
field, I can't play my trap cards.

8
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:16,197
That means my alligator sword will be
easy pickings for this psycho fraud.

9
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:20,809
Then I'll have to kiss my life points
and the Battle City Tournament goodbye.

10
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:23,240
It's time to end this duel.

11
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:27,680
So I'll play this, the
magic card Amplifier.

12
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:31,040
And now I'll hardwire it to Jinzo,

13
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:35,000
which will immediately boost
his attack power by 500 points.

14
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:43,340
Plus, with every new turn, Amplifier will
crank up Jinzo's power by 300 more points.

15
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,330
Oh, no.

16
00:01:44,413 --> 00:01:49,400
And now, my metal monster, send his
alligator sword back to the swamp!

17
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:58,740
I foresee the end for you!

18
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:02,737
If you think I'm giving up just
because of Baldi and his tin can hat,

19
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:06,526
you definitely got another thing
coming, you blue-haired freak!

20
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:10,140
I'll crush you even without
my brother's help! Yay!

21
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:11,530
You rock!

22
00:02:11,613 --> 00:02:12,797
Go, go, go, brother!

23
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:13,840
Oh, right.

24
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:16,517
Even without us giving him
the info, Esper's winning.

25
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:20,080
And he's still faking the ESP
just to psych that guy out.

26
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:24,340
Ah, Esper-Oba's a strong duelist,
but I know Joey can beat him.

27
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:27,750
Right.

28
00:02:27,833 --> 00:02:29,980
This duel isn't over yet. Ha-ha!

29
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,557
But I predict it will be just
as soon as I make my next move.

30
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:36,137
Why not just give me
your locator card now?

31
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:37,540
Bad chance, Roba.

32
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:40,737
You and your psychic fraud
network are about to go down.

33
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:41,650
Check this out.

34
00:02:41,733 --> 00:02:44,080
All right, come on, baby.

35
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:45,860
Deck, don't fail me now.

36
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:50,020
Yes, my old friend, Baby Dragon.

37
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,940
Joey's back in business.

38
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:53,330
Ha-ha!

39
00:02:53,413 --> 00:02:54,257
Give it up, Wheeler.

40
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:57,060
My Jinzo already has 2,900 attack points,

41
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:01,597
and my cosmic forces tell me he's already
stronger than any card in your deck.

42
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:04,386
Plus, Jinzo's only going
to get more powerful.

43
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:08,180
I'll keep that in mind
as I summon Baby Dragon.

44
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:15,620
I know what you're up to.

45
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,566
It's the same trick
Wheeler used to defeat me.

46
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:23,557
I don't know whether I should attack
your monster or give it a baby bottle.

47
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:27,377
But if that's the best that you've got
to face, Jinzo, then you're finished.

48
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:32,107
It may be just a baby now, but it's
possible that my dragon's about to grow up.

49
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:36,740
Cause I summon Time
Wizard. Time Wizard? I see.

50
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:40,857
You're gonna try to age that
baby dragon into an older dragon.

51
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:41,800
Maybe.

52
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:46,277
Well, my telepathic powers are telling
me that that still won't be enough.

53
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,680
It's gonna be a risk.

54
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:50,657
But if Time Wizard's spinner
lands in the right place,

55
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:52,077
a thousand years will pass,

56
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:56,160
making my dragon stronger and
aging his ginzo into scrap metal.

57
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:59,720
Okay, let's find out
if luck is on my side.

58
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:02,560
Come on.

59
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:03,700
Not a skull.

60
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,140
That'll destroy my life points.

61
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:10,817
All right!

62
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:12,076
It's Time Warp time!

63
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:18,280
Baby Dragon ages a thousand years
to reemerge as Thousand Dragons!

64
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:27,377
Now, here's the part
of the plan you missed.

65
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:30,401
Your metal monster rusting
into a heap of scratch!

66
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:34,460
What the heck?

67
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,000
Hey, where's the rust?

68
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,200
Some flat dork.

69
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:41,092
What's the matter, Joey?

70
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:43,717
Jinso's special armor
took you by surprise?

71
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:48,960
My monster is made of a special dyed
titanium metal that's guaranteed not to age,

72
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,360
rust, or corrode for 10,000 years.

73
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,900
Died titanium who?

74
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,617
You should have done your homework.

75
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:56,540
Come on, Joey.

76
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:57,760
Stay focused.

77
00:04:58,080 --> 00:04:59,640
You can beat this guy.

78
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,980
We both know it.

79
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,757
You're mine, Wheeler.

80
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:07,440
Now Jinso, attack his Thousand
Dragon with Cyber Energy Shock!

81
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:16,440
Now that my dragon's gone,
how long can I hold on?

82
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,160
Come on, Joey.

83
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:26,637
With this secret weapon gone,
Joey's just barely holding on.

84
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:29,080
Hey Tristan, you've been awfully quiet.

85
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,260
My brother is still
winning the duel, right?

86
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,230
Um, yeah.

87
00:05:34,313 --> 00:05:38,040
I mean, uh, you see, he's sort
of, um, what was the question?

88
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,060
Joey's not losing, is he? Um, no.

89
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:43,440
No, don't be silly. It's cool.

90
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,237
He's just toying with his opponent.

91
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,150
Oh, okay.

92
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:49,660
Thank you for letting me
know exactly what's going on.

93
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:52,720
I can't tell Serenity that Joey's losing.

94
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:54,414
It'll break her heart.

95
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,757
Time for me to take your temperature.

96
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:02,700
Oh, I'll just step outside and
take in a little fresh air. Okay.

97
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:05,800
See ya.

98
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,860
You gotta win, Joey.

99
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,657
Otherwise, you're out of the tournament.

100
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:13,564
Well, we're all behind
you, especially Serenity.

101
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:15,540
Hmm, that gives me an idea.

102
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:19,757
Looks to me like you're doing
extremely well, Serenity.

103
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:23,320
Um, nurse, can you help
me? Of course. The duel.

104
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:27,935
Could you take a look at the screen
and tell me who's winning right now?

105
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,190
Uh, hmm.

106
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,428
What's your brother's name?

107
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:39,980
All that talk about ancient evil
forces returning is freaking me out.

108
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,280
Guess who?

109
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,340
Hey, you scared me!

110
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:45,740
I scared you?

111
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,560
That noggin of yours
almost broke my schnoz!

112
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:51,080
Well, don't sneak up on me!

113
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:52,530
Huh?

114
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,320
This is Taya.

115
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:56,961
Hey-ya, Tristan!

116
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:59,574
Are you watching Joey's duel right now?

117
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,060
No, I'm not.

118
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:02,360
What's going on?

119
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,070
Find him.

120
00:07:04,153 --> 00:07:06,238
You've got to give him this message.

121
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:09,280
Your Battle City days are over, Wheeler!

122
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:14,345
Your dragon is destroyed, and according
to the celestial forces that tell me all,

123
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,497
you have nothing in your
hand that can defeat Jinzo!

124
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:18,980
Your future looks dim!

125
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:21,740
As long as I have my deck, I have hope.

126
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:25,697
It didn't let me down at Duel's
Kingdom, and it won't let me down here.

127
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:27,860
Activate the Magic Card Scapegoat!

128
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,794
That's your best move?

129
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:36,337
Those hairballs can't
save your life points.

130
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:38,197
Jinzo will take them out one by one.

131
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,720
Then he'll destroy you.

132
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,817
Why don't you make it easier on yourself,

133
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:44,417
Wheeler, and just hand
me your locator card?

134
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:49,100
Or you can just continue to embarrass
yourself by playing lame cards.

135
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,617
The little creep's right, Wheeler.

136
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:54,157
This duel's as good as over.

137
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,220
I mean, come on.

138
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,457
Even I couldn't defeat his Jinzo.

139
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,140
It's your move, Groba.

140
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,520
I warn ya.

141
00:08:02,540 --> 00:08:03,893
We're all finished now.

142
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:05,393
Then I'll head back in.

143
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:11,200
Tristan? That's me.

144
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:13,437
Bet you're wanting a duel update, eh?

145
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:16,285
Joey's probably still
stringing that guy along.

146
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,180
Wait, it's okay.

147
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,500
Thank you, Tristan, really.

148
00:08:21,780 --> 00:08:25,300
But you don't have to
continue lying to me. Huh?

149
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:29,160
I asked the nurse to tell
me what's been going on.

150
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:32,380
I know Joey's been losing
this duel the whole time.

151
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:34,500
Sorry, Serenity.

152
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:38,192
I just didn't want you to be
worried about Joey, you know?

153
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,557
That's so sweet.

154
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,400
But I have to know the
truth about my brother.

155
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:45,097
If he's in some kind of trouble,
I want to be told about it.

156
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:49,057
He's always been there for me when I needed
him, and now I need to be there for him.

157
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:51,697
On the day of my eye
surgery, I was so scared.

158
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:55,721
I couldn't go through with it until
Joey got there and stood by me.

159
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:59,060
My big brother's never let me down.

160
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:02,740
Now it's my turn to do
whatever I can to help out.

161
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:04,500
I guess you're right.

162
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:09,602
I may not be next to him, but can you help
me be with him in spirit, pretty please?

163
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,420
You bet I can.

164
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:15,457
Now let's get back to the duel and cheer
that brother of yours till he wins.

165
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:16,370
Great.

166
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,797
All right, tough guy.

167
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:19,233
Let's see what you got.

168
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:26,457
you're just prolonging
your defeat wheeler but

169
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,540
if that's what you want
who am i to stop you

170
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:31,920
it's my move

171
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:37,980
i summon reflex founder to the field

172
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:46,417
my new monster is practically
attack proof it can

173
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:49,794
reflect any of your monster's
attacks right back at you.

174
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,997
So even if you did manage
to summon a decent monster,

175
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:55,857
all of your attacks would
be completely useless.

176
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:57,420
Bring it on.

177
00:09:57,700 --> 00:09:59,240
And don't forget,

178
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:00,657
with this in every turn,

179
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:04,780
amplifier increases Jindal's
attack power by another 300 points.

180
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:09,880
Now I've got two undefeatable
monsters on the field.

181
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:12,740
And you, you don't have a chance, Wheeler.

182
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:20,760
Now, Jinzo, attack your scapegoat!

183
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:28,171
Reflect founder, it's your turn to attack!

184
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:34,037
Your future's looking more
pathetic by the second.

185
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:37,897
Two scapegoats are down, and if my
extra sensory perception is right,

186
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:40,215
the other two will meet the same fate.

187
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:43,857
Sorry, I don't mean to
laugh at you, Wheeler.

188
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:47,237
Losing like this must be painful, but
I'm afraid it's going to get worse.

189
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:50,337
By my next turn, I'll have
three monsters on the field,

190
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:53,300
and I predict your life
points will be gone!

191
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,600
What a pathetic way to end your
Battle City experience. Ha!

192
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:02,817
You couldn't even make your
way out of the first round!

193
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:05,665
I can't lose like this,
but what else can I do?

194
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:08,280
Come on, Wheeler! Face the facts!

195
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:13,300
With those cards, your future career as
a duelist is bleak and getting bleaker.

196
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,660
I can't listen to him.

197
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,900
Hang in there, Joey.

198
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:23,820
You can beat him.

199
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:27,544
Why don't you hand me
your rare time wizard now?

200
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:28,681
You're finished.

201
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:31,040
Maybe this guy's right.

202
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:35,205
I mean, I've played my best cards,
and they weren't good enough.

203
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:39,020
If I lose, he gets my only
locator card and my time wizard,

204
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:40,537
so I'll be out of the tournament.

205
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:41,820
I guess it is over.

206
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:43,740
Joey, hang in there. Huh?

207
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,380
Excuse me. Hey, Joey!

208
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:48,550
Taya!

209
00:11:49,140 --> 00:11:51,081
Tristan called from the hospital.

210
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:54,957
He's watching the duel on the
internet right now with Serenity.

211
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,746
Your sister wants you
to know something, Joey.

212
00:11:58,100 --> 00:11:59,140
What is it?

213
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:00,500
What did she say?

214
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,860
You two are a team. Forever.

215
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:08,160
And she believes in you, so
don't even think about giving up.

216
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,447
There's no way I'm quitting.

217
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:17,232
Serenity would never give up on me,
and I'm not about to give up on myself.

218
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:20,017
I know you're right here with me, sis.

219
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:22,137
So I'm gonna win this duel with your help.

220
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:25,102
This so-called psychic
clown is about to go down.

221
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,257
Enough stalling!

222
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:29,057
Are you gonna quit or what, Wheeler?

223
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:30,280
I don't think so.

224
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,190
Really?

225
00:12:32,273 --> 00:12:33,103
Suit yourself!

226
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:34,458
That's right, Joey.

227
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,580
You can still win this duel.

228
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:41,877
You just have to believe in yourself
and in the heart of the cards.

229
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,240
I know I can do this.

230
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:45,877
The odds are against me,
but my friends are with me.

231
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,500
I gotta have faith.

232
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:50,617
I know there's a card in
my deck that could help me.

233
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:52,877
A card that could turn this thing around.

234
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:57,120
Now all I gotta do is draw it so
I can finish Esperoba. Come on.

235
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:58,880
Trust your deck, Joey.

236
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:01,600
Roba, check this out.

237
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:03,710
Yes!

238
00:13:03,793 --> 00:13:06,120
The magic card, Rulet Spider.

239
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:11,060
Rulet Spider, attach to Jinzo.

240
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,420
Ah! What's that?

241
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:16,790
Ah!

242
00:13:16,873 --> 00:13:18,186
What's the point of all this?

243
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:21,637
Playing Roulette Spider is one of
the riskiest moves in Duel Monsters.

244
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:24,249
It could destroy me or
win the duel for me.

245
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:27,037
You see, after I give up
half of my life points,

246
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:28,817
Roulette Spider blindfolds the strongest

247
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:31,637
monster on the field and
walks it to the center.

248
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,661
That's where it gets interesting.

249
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:37,240
What is that web for, Wheeler?

250
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:40,365
For a guy with ESP, you
ask a lot of questions.

251
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:41,737
That's the spin table.

252
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:44,697
My spider will spin Ginzo round
and round like a giant wheel.

253
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,217
When you tell it to stop,

254
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:49,377
it'll automatically attack whichever
target the arrow's pointing to.

255
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:50,480
Any target?

256
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:52,680
Open your ears, Psycho Boy.

257
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:53,800
Any target.

258
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:57,822
Could be me, or you directly, or
any of the monsters on the field.

259
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:00,017
And since you've been
so good about piling up

260
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:01,997
attack points for your
monster friend there,

261
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:05,198
whatever Jinzo points to
will be destroyed instantly.

262
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,160
Any predictions, Mr. ESP?

263
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,240
But I...

264
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:11,397
What's Wheeler thinking?

265
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:16,137
That lame brain's about to risk losing
and getting kicked out of the tournament.

266
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,900
This move will never work.

267
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:19,710
Ready?

268
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:22,260
Go, Roulette Spider! Spin now!

269
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:33,780
Whatever it points to, it destroys.

270
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,720
What's the matter, Fraud?

271
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:38,900
You too scared to tell it to stop?

272
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,180
Easy for him to say.

273
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:44,717
With such a lame deck,
he's got nothing to lose.

274
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,212
If Jinso points to me, I lose everything.

275
00:14:58,140 --> 00:14:59,740
I believe in you, Joey.

276
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,340
What you waiting for?

277
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:11,220
Ahh, Jindo! Stop!

278
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:25,600
Jindo's pointing to my Reflect Bounder,
and if it attacks, they're both doomed!

279
00:15:30,460 --> 00:15:32,260
Ahh! Don't reflect!

280
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,581
He'll send his attack right back!

281
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:38,760
No, you can't!

282
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:43,429
If Jizzle's flask is bounced back to it
by reflex founder, they're both gone!

283
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:56,060
Too late, Rover.

284
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:59,499
Both your monsters are
destroyed and you're history!

285
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,880
No, I had it won!

286
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:04,290
I...

287
00:16:04,373 --> 00:16:05,300
you couldn't beat me.

288
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:06,857
What do you think just happened?

289
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:09,617
Let me do the math for
you, you psychic sneak.

290
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:12,000
Jinzo started with 3,200 attack points.

291
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:14,160
Subtract Reflect Bound to 1,700.

292
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:17,020
And you lose 1,500 life points.

293
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:20,640
You're finished.

294
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:22,420
And his duel is over.

295
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:23,970
Yeah!

296
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,340
He did it!

297
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:29,364
What an amazing comeback, Joey.

298
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:31,020
I just knew it.

299
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:32,200
I knew he'd win.

300
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:35,500
Nice work!

301
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:42,557
Esper put up an awesome
fight, but that guy beat him!

302
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,120
He was so close!

303
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,240
He beat me!

304
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,860
Check out the Psychic Duelist now!

305
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,457
What happened to his ESB?

306
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:53,658
He couldn't predict he'd be a loser!

307
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:56,880
It was a tough duel.

308
00:16:57,200 --> 00:17:00,340
Now fork over your Jinzo
and your Locator card!

309
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:02,310
No!

310
00:17:02,393 --> 00:17:03,223
I can't!

311
00:17:03,306 --> 00:17:04,377
Please don't make me!

312
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:05,989
You just don't understand!

313
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:10,537
What are you freaking out about?

314
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:12,385
Just stand up and face defeat.

315
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:14,837
Besides, you know the battle city rules.

316
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,744
I get to keep your rarest card.

317
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,784
Everyone loses once in a while.

318
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:21,517
Even Joey Wheeler blew
a few duels in his day.

319
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:23,080
But it's not that simple!

320
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,480
People count on me to win, Wheeler!

321
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:28,213
We all have our own reasons for dueling.

322
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:29,557
Stop!

323
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:32,020
You just don't get it, do you?

324
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:33,712
Losing is not an option.

325
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:36,220
I have to win at all costs. I must.

326
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,917
I'm not dueling for myself.

327
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,647
I'm dueling for my brothers.

328
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:40,870
Brothers?

329
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:43,040
My little brothers look up to me.

330
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,620
I'm like a hero to them.

331
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:50,160
If my reputation as a loser spreads,
they'll get picked on by bullies again.

332
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:52,320
That's crazy talk, Roba.

333
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:56,700
Trust me, this duelist knows a few
things about being a big brother.

334
00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:58,560
Come on, huh?

335
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,760
You need a hand?

336
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,100
I don't need your pity!

337
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:08,500
Fine, be that way.

338
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:12,120
Come on, big bro, get up! What?

339
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:13,877
Where's that voice coming from?

340
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,417
You didn't disappoint us.

341
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:19,029
You fought an awesome duel, and
you did it without cheating.

342
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:20,632
We're proud of you, bro.

343
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:22,577
But I lost. So?

344
00:18:22,660 --> 00:18:27,366
Oh, so you're not worried about people
thinking your big brother is a big loser?

345
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:30,200
No, because in our book, you're a winner.

346
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,920
Well, come here and give your bro a hug.

347
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:38,760
Thank you, guys.

348
00:18:39,180 --> 00:18:41,920
I guess I have a lot
to learn about winning.

349
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:44,120
You duel great.

350
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:47,737
And the totally best part of
it is you did it on your own.

351
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:50,817
Yeah, without using any
of that phony ESP stuff.

352
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:54,820
So I guess these guys are the
cosmic forces he was talking to.

353
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:59,002
Now all I need is his rare Jinzo
card to finish this happy ending.

354
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:03,057
Good work, Joey.

355
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:05,140
I knew you'd find your strength.

356
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:13,510
Here.

357
00:19:13,593 --> 00:19:15,360
My Jinzo and my Locator card.

358
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:16,920
You deserve them.

359
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:18,550
Thanks.

360
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:21,740
Look, I'm sorry about that cheating thing.

361
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,560
Ah, no worries.

362
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:28,900
You beat me fair and square, and next
time we duel, I'm playing totally legit.

363
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:30,300
No more cheating.

364
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:32,200
I'll hold you to that.

365
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:35,109
Until then, smell you
later, Robo-Brothers.

366
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:38,680
You know, we're a lot alike, Esper.

367
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:40,170
Huh?

368
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:44,300
You've got your brothers, and
I've got my sister and my pals,

369
00:19:44,460 --> 00:19:47,517
and we're all there to support
each other when we need it.

370
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:50,340
As long as we got that, nobody loses.

371
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:53,940
See you later.

372
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,477
Excellent dueling, Joey.

373
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:58,000
Yeah, way to go. Thanks.

374
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:06,180
Joey did great today.

375
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,304
He gets better with every duel.

376
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:10,935
Well, my first duel of the tournament.

377
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:13,557
And not a bad start,
if I do say so myself.

378
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:14,737
There'll be tough times ahead.

379
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:17,080
But I know I'm not in this alone.
